flowchart TD
    A([Issue in Triage]) --> B[Owner bot writes options]
    B --> C{Human decides<br/>in a comment}
    C -->|owner bot has questions| Q[Questions on the issue,<br/>issue stays in Triage]
    Q --> C
    C -->|brief written| D[Card to Backlog,<br/>coordinator starts worker]
    D --> D2[Worker pushes<br/>a first commit]
    D2 --> D3[Coordinator opens draft PR<br/>with a closing link,<br/>issue card to Active]
    D3 --> E[Worker pushes code and tests<br/>to the draft PR]
    E --> F{Coordinator<br/>pre-check}
    F -->|fails| E
    F -->|passes| G[Mark ready,<br/>card to Auto Review]
    G --> H{Automated review,<br/>round within the limit}
    H -->|P1 or P2 finding| I[Back to draft, In Progress,<br/>worker fixes the root cause,<br/>neighboring cases + tests]
    I --> J[Coordinator examines the fix,<br/>resolves the thread]
    J -->|under the limit| G
    J -->|limit reached:<br/>coordinator examines,<br/>no more automated rounds| K
    H -->|clean| K{Coordinator<br/>post-check}
    K -->|fails| I
    K -->|passes| RQ[Ready,<br/>not on the staging environment]
    RQ -->|Staging below target:<br/>pull one at a time| L[Merge into staging,<br/>deploy staging,<br/>verify served commit,<br/>screenshots in the PR if visible]
    L --> M{Gate into Staging}
    M -->|passes| P[Staging,<br/>3 to 5]
    P -->|Human Review slot opens,<br/>card move| N[Human Review,<br/>exactly two]
    M -->|fails| I
    N -->|human moves card to In Progress,<br/>or late finding| I
    N -->|human merges| O([Main])
